      "directNodeIds": [
        "cnm_p184",
        "cnm_p173"
      ],
      "explanation": "The four added gallons fill the difference between one-half and one-third of the tank. That fraction is\n\\[\n\\frac12-\\frac13=\\frac36-\\frac26=\\frac16.\n\\]\nThus one-sixth of the tank holds \\(4\\) gallons. A full tank contains six of these equal portions, so its capacity is\n\\[\n6\\cdot4=24\\text{ gallons}.\n\\]\nThe answer is \\(24\\) gallons, choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{D}}\\).",
